DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((cos((e^(x)))))^2");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln(((x^2-2*x+4)^2+3*(x^2-1*x+1)+4))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 12] U [4, infinity) U [4, infinity)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("[4, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 12]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 12]))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(([0, 12])) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -6, 0, 2, 6, 9}) U (((([0, 12]))))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(({-10, -6, 0, 2, 6, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-10, -6, 0, 2, 6, 9})))) - {-10, -6, 0, 2, 6, 9})");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[0, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [0, 12]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -6, 0, 2, 6, 9})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`8+5+7-3/15`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(19.8),width=>8}
---

What is the value of [`16/19+0`]? [_____]{0.842105263158}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 0 \leq x \leq 12\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -6, 0, 2, 6, 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`((A)) \cap B \cup ((((A)))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B \cap ((B))) - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 12\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 4\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cap A \cap (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -1, 4, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, 10, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -1, -2, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-1, 4, 4>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, 4, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, 4, 4>") . Compute("<-1, -2, -8>")}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -2, -8>") . Compute("<-1, 4, 4>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, 10, -3>") x Compute("<-1, -2, -8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -2, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, 3, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -6, 2, 0 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, 3, -6>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, 3, -6>") x Compute("<-6, 2, 0>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, 2, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, 3, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, 3, -6>") . Compute("<-6, 2, 0>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, 2, 0>") x Compute("<10, 3, -6>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
